From bef2a3a881b3e952426459803e50c433da2f0195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:14:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Memory accounting by category (RUFFLE_MEMLOG), sampled
 by ruffle_sdl

The tool that found where a large AVM1 game spent its 800
MB, kept so the next memory problem on a handheld can be measured the same
way. Off by default: a disabled tag is an inert value and costs one branch.

* ruffle_render::memlog: a Tag adds its size to a category while it lives
  and keeps a short description of the item. Categories: BitmapData CPU
  pixels, BitmapData textures, SWF bitmap textures, cacheAsBitmap textures,
  pooled render targets, shape meshes (split into those first tessellated
  inside BitmapData.draw and the rest), sounds copied into the mixer, the
  uncompressed SWF, and library data kept for the life of the movie (parsed
  shape records, compressed bitmaps). A thread-local context ("bitmapdata",
  "bitmapdata.draw") tells the wgpu backend who asked for a texture or mesh.
  GPU to CPU readbacks are counted too.
* Hooks: BitmapRawData pixels, wgpu Texture (register_bitmap,
  create_empty_texture), the texture pool, Mesh, mixer sounds, bitmap
  characters, shape records, SwfMovie (logs its size once).
* ruffle_sdl: with RUFFLE_MEMLOG=1 a thread samples VmRSS, RssAnon and
  RssFile every RUFFLE_MEMLOG_MS (100) ms and logs once a second (target
  memlog, so RUST_LOG needs memlog=info) the highest sample with the
  category totals, the C heap use and the gc object count
  (Player::gc_count). At every new RSS peak the biggest items of each
  category (RUFFLE_MEMLOG_TOP, 8) are written to the file RUFFLE_MEMLOG_PEAK,
  or logged. The C heap figures come from mallinfo2, looked up at run time
  with dlsym because the handhelds have glibc older than 2.33; mallinfo is
  the fallback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
